# Full-resolution reviewer frames are evidence ON DISK, not in git.
#
# A Codex review drops one ~6MB full-screen PNG per screen it looks at — 15 of
# them is 69MB for a single round, and they accumulate every round. The frames
# that a finding actually depends on are committed by name (see the
# `evidence-*/` directories), because a claim like "this row printed its text
# twice" is worth nothing six months later without the frame that shows it.
#
# Everything else here is re-derivable: the reviewer writes the same URL and seed
# again, and the screens are deterministic.
evidence-*/
!evidence-*/
evidence-*/*-review.png
!evidence-*/city-arena-entry-review.png
!evidence-*/city-federal-gap-review.png
!evidence-*/arena-menu-after-fix.png
!evidence-*/arena-rows-after-fix.json
# Playwright's own per-run temp frames.
_small_arena.png
_small_arena.png-*.png
